eeff7ad5c2b743d","ma-c-9803b90238c238a4bdef","ma-c-9abf68b0c1467e774ac1","ma-c-a37c8be71b65474212ef","ma-c-a733facf0af51a016dea","ma-c-a820eb59a35fc8d820e8","ma-c-aa3b6b715ace6362e131","ma-c-acba74833281717830b0","ma-c-b4f1790e775459171ece","ma-c-bd8b5599769e7aa58299","ma-c-be75e65100daf4dbb3ea","ma-c-bfe831ed6147fcac00bb","ma-c-cad79ada6fc1674974f7","ma-c-ce26411e2551afbb6e59","ma-c-cf2611faf2f23b28bfa5","ma-c-d07d4cbfe5567a7c3da0","ma-c-d2c568063d38e3439ad4","ma-c-db7127892025a8ca58f6","ma-c-dd33870951f474525a11","ma-c-e2f8aa5750fdf998340c","ma-c-e921388722572fe53501","ma-c-ea2f7f347da83804c0db","ma-c-eab6194a8b09c7195a9b","ma-c-ed7028356571e381c691","ma-c-ef8c5c24a1809dc9f1e7","ma-c-f25223e55e09fabc081e","ma-c-f50e6603976d4ed0b4e9","ma-c-fa7030b7952df5667cd9","ma-c-fbd8d6c87454fdf83c02"],"papers":{"arXiv:1105.2160":{"abstract":"V.I. Arnold [Russian Math. Surveys 26(2) (1971) 29-43] constructed a miniversal deformation of a square complex matrix under similarity; that is, a simple normal form to which not only a given square matrix A but all matrices B close to it can be reduced by similarity transformations that smoothly depend on the entries of B. We give miniversal deformations of matrices of sesquilinear forms; that i","authors":["A. Dmytryshyn","V. Futorny","V. V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:0710.0928":{"abstract":"We give canonical matrices of bilinear or sesquilinear forms UxV-->C, (V/U)xV-->C, in which V is a vector space over the field C of complex numbers and U is its subspace.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1304.5762":{"abstract":"We study how small perturbations of a 2-by-2 complex matrix can change its canonical form for *congruence. We construct the Hasse diagram for the closure ordering on the set of *congruence classes of 2-by-2 matrices.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Lena Klimenko","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2013"},"arXiv:1004.3590":{"abstract":"We construct the Hasse diagrams $G_2$ and $G_3$ for the closure ordering on the sets of congruence classes of $2\\times 2$ and $3\\times 3$ complex matrices. In other words, we construct two directed graphs whose vertices are $2\\times 2$ or, respectively, $3\\times 3$ canonical matrices under congruence and there is a directed path from $A$ to $B$ if and only if $A$ can be transformed by an arbitrari","authors":["Andrii Dmytryshyn","Vyacheslav Futorny","Bo Kågström"],"year":"2010"},"arXiv:1112.3682":{"abstract":"A square matrix is nonderogatory if its Jordan blocks have distinct eigenvalues. We give canonical forms (i) for nonderogatory complex matrices up to unitary similarity and (ii) for pairs of complex matrices up to similarity, in which one matrix has distinct eigenvalues. The types of these canonical forms are given by undirected and, respectively, directed graphs with no undirected cycles.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2011"},"arXiv:0710.0810":{"abstract":"Tridiagonal canonical forms of square matrices under congruence or *congruence, pairs of symmetric or skew-symmetric matrices under congruence, and pairs of Hermitian matrices under *congruence are given over an algebraically closed field of characteristic different from 2.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:0710.0954":{"abstract":"We give a canonical form for a complex matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of unitary similarity as well as a canonical form for a real matrix, whose square is normal, under transformations of orthogonal similarity.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Roger A. Horn","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2007"},"arXiv:1907.03213":{"abstract":"Our purpose is to give new proofs of several known results about perturbations of matrix pencils. Andrzej Pokrzywa (1986) described the closure of orbit of a Kronecker canonical pencil $A-λB$ in terms of inequalities with pencil invariants. In more detail, Pokrzywa described all Kronecker canonical pencils $K-λL$ such that each neighborhood of $A-λB$ contains a pencil whose Kronecker canonical for","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Klymchuk","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2019"},"arXiv:1810.09219":{"abstract":"In representation theory, a classification problem is called wild if it contains the problem of classifying matrix pairs up to simultaneous similarity. The latter problem is considered as hopeless; it contains the problem of classifying an arbitrary finite system of vector spaces and linear mappings between them. We prove that an analogous \"universal\" problem in the theory of tensors of order at m","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Joshua A. Grochow","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2018"},"arXiv:1403.2645":{"abstract":"We give a method for constructing a regularizing decomposition of a matrix pencil, which is formulated in terms of the linear mappings. We prove that two pencils are topologically equivalent if and only if their regularizing decompositions coincide up to permutation of summands and their regular parts coincide up to homeomorphisms of their spaces.","authors":["Vyacheslav Futorny","Tetiana Rybalkina","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2014"},"arXiv:1911.04993":{"abstract":"Let $V$ be a vector space over a field $\\mathbb F$ with scalar product given by a nondegenerate sesquilinear form whose matrix is diagonal in some basis. If $\\mathbb F=\\mathbb C$, then we give canonical matrices of isometric and selfadjoint operators on $V$ using known classifications of isometric and selfadjoint operators on a complex vector space with nondegenerate Hermitian form. If $\\mathbb F$","authors":["Jonathan V. Caalim","Vyacheslav Futorny","Vladimir V. Sergeichuk"],"year":"2019"},"arXiv:1208.5418":{"abstract":"We give a canonical form of matrices of a cycle of linear or semilinear mapping V_1 --- V_2 --- ... --- V_t --- V_1 in which all V_i are complex vector spaces, each line is an arrow ---> or <---, and each arrow denotes a linear or semilinear mapping.","authors":["Debora Duarte de Oliveira","Vyacheslav Futorny","Tatiana Klimchuk"],"year":"2012"}}}